sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Body and senses
    participant M as Causal temporal state
    participant P as Intention and learned policy
    participant F as Forward and self models
    participant W as Internal wellness and value
    participant R as Real experience
    B->>M: New tilt, motion, touch, images, function and command age
    M->>P: Observed history, bodily condition and previous intention
    loop Internal imagined continuations from the same starting state
        P->>F: Chosen goal and coordinated body, eye and finger request
        Note over P,F: Same command conversion as the body, no fall or get-up script
        F->>M: Predict next motion, contacts, sensations and local function
        M->>W: Advance branch history and measured-meaning wellness inputs
        W->>P: Expected retained control minus deficit, effort and sharp pain
        Note over M,W: Repeat through three seconds, then add learned continuation value
    end
    P->>P: Rank intrinsic expected wellness across sampled outcomes
    P->>B: Send first short request of the best internally imagined continuation
    Note over B,P: Same learned policy for ordinary motion, disturbance and recovery
    B->>M: Fresh actual readings update the next decision
    B->>R: Effective action, duration, pain severity increment, event ID and body function
    R->>F: Earlier prefix plus actual command sequence learns later pain and function targets
    R->>W: Immediate sharp-pain penalty and ongoing wellness teach one-step TD value
    W->>P: One-step TD updates value, actor learns from changed value
    Note over B,R: Sequence pain prediction can improve before value backups reach every earlier choice
    Note over M,F: Past and same-time senses may combine, later measured answers stay out of earlier inputs
